A safer approach might be to check if `res.send` or `res.json` methods are available, and if I detect an API client, I call `res.status(404).json(...)` before the request falls through entirely. But Express routing logic already determines if a route exists. If we reach `app.handle` and `finalhandler` is called, it means no route matched.

I will replace the call to `finalhandler` in `lib/application.js` with a custom handler that respects API clients.

