In `lib/application.js`:

```javascript
// Around line 15Now I need to design the change. The plan: in app.handle, wrap the default finalhandler: when the router finishes with no error and the client does not accept HTML, reply res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not Found' }); otherwise delegate to finalhandler.

But careful: finalhandler handles errors too. The wrapper should only intercept the "no error" case (404 not found) and only when the client doesn't accept HTML. Also should only do this when no callback provided (default final handler). Also need to consider HEAD requests? JSON body for HEAD would be suppressed by res.json? Actually res.json sends body; for HEAD, express's res.send handles HEAD by not sending body? Let's check lib/response.js send: it checks `if (req.method === 'HEAD') { this.end() }`. Yes express handles HEAD.

