In Command:
- `this._envPrefix = undefined;` in constructor
- `envPrefix(prefix)` method: sets `this._envPrefix = prefix; return this;`
- copyInheritedSettings: `this._envPrefix = sourceCommand._envPrefix;`
- In `addOption` (or `option()`), if `this._envPrefix` and option has no envVar, set `option.envVar = this._envPrefix + option.name().toUpperCase().replace(/-/g, '_')`? Actual implementation: I recall in Commander's command.js:

```js
  addOption(option) {
    ...
    if (this._envPrefix && !option.envVar) {
      option.env(envVarName(this._envPrefix, option));
    }
```

Hmm, let me recall the actual v14 code. I believe:

```js
  /**
   * Set the prefix for environment variables for options.
   *
   * @param {string} prefix
   * @return {Command} `this` command for chaining
   */
  envPrefix(prefix) {
    this._envPrefix = prefix;
    return this;
  }
```

and in addOption:

```js
    if (this._envPrefix && !option.envVar) {
