Hmm, attributeName is camelCase; uppercase gives `FOO_BAR`? No — camelCase `fooBar` uppercased is `FOOBAR`. So they'd need to convert. I think actual implementation used `option.name().toUpperCase().replace(/-/g, '_')`. Let me search the web to confirm the real API and semantics — worth one research call to match upstream naming/behaviour (help output, negated options, etc.).

Actually, let me just check the real Commander source. I'll do a quick web search/read of the commander docs for envPrefix.

