message.reasoning:
So the repo already has Option.env() and _parseOptionsEnv. The feature request: make it easier to configure options from environment — i.e. add `envPrefix` on Command so env var names are derived automatically from long flags.

This is the actual commander v13 feature: `program.envPrefix('MYAPP')` — options get env var `MYAPP_FOO` derived from long flag. Let me recall the real implementation in commander v13:

In lib/option.js:
```js
  /**
   * Set environment variable to check for option value.
   *
   * An environment variable is only used if when processed the current option value is
   * undefined, or the source of the current value is 'default' or 'config' or 'env'.
   *
   * @param {string} name
   * @return {Option}
   */

  env(name) {
    this.envVar = name;
    return this;
  }
```
And in v13, `_parseOptionsEnv` in command.js:

```js
  _parseOptionsEnv() {
    this.options.forEach((option) => {
      if (option.envVar && option.envVar in process.env) {
        ...
      }
    });
  }
```

Actually the real v13 implementation: Command has `envPrefix(prefix)`:

```js
  /**
   * Set the prefix for the environment variables for options.
   *
   * @param {string} prefix
   * @return {Command} `this` command for chaining
   */

  envPrefix(prefix) {
    this._envPrefix = prefix;
    return this;
  }
```

And in `_registerOption` / `addOption`, when option has no envVar and command has _envPrefix, derive:

Real commander v13 code (from memory of lib/command.js):

