So env support already exists via option.env(name). The feature request: make it easier to configure options from environment — i.e. envPrefix on command, deriving env var names automatically.

Let me check the actual commander upstream implementation (v13 has envPrefix). Let me look at how upstream did it. In commander v13, `Command.envPrefix(prefix)` sets `_envPrefix`, and `Option` has `envVar` derived... Actually upstream v13.0.0 added `envPrefix` and `Option.env()`; the automatic derivation from long flag: in `_registerOption`? Let me recall: commander v13 `command.envPrefix('MYAPP')` then options get env var `MYAPP_DRY_RUN` automatically. Implementation in lib/option.js:

```js
  /**
   * Set environment variable to check for option value.
   *
   * An environment variable is only used if when processed the current option value is
   * undefined, or the source of the current value is 'default' or 'config' or 'env'.
   *
   * @param {string} name
   * @return {Option}
   */
  env(name) {
    this.envVar = name;
    return this;
  }
```

