Careful: `done` is also the callback when the app is mounted (next(err) from parent). In app.handle, `callback` is provided when mounted; then the mounted app's failure is passed to parent. Hmm: if a mounted app has no matching route, `app.handle(req,res,callback)` gets callback from the mounted_app wrapper which calls `next(err)` on the parent router, so the parent continues. In that case we should NOT respond JSON in the sub-app (the parent may still match another route). But if the parent also fails, the top-level app.handle's finalhandler (no callback) will run, and we can respond JSON there. Good: only apply the JSON 404 in the case where we use finalhandler (i.e., no callback), i.e., top-most app.

