message.reasoning:
I need to stop probing and make the change. Design:

In `lib/application.js`, `app.handle` creates `done = callback || finalhandler(...)`. I need to intercept the not-found case (no error) and, if `req.accepts(['html','json']) === 'json'`, respond with JSON 404 instead of delegating to finalhandler.

Implementation: wrap the finalhandler callback:

```js
app.handle = function handle(req, res, callback) {
  // final handler
  var done = callback || finalhandler(req, res, {
    env: this.get('env'),
    onerror: logerror.bind(this)
  });
  ...
```

I'll add a `notFound`-aware done:

```js
var finalHandler = callback || finalhandler(...);
var done = callback || function (err) {
  if (err || !prefersJson(req)) return finalHandler(err);
  // JSON 404
  ...
