Behavior: wrapper around done; if err is falsy (404) and req.accepts(['html','json']) === 'json', respond JSON body {error:'Not Found', method, path}. Path: the full path the client asked for, inside mounted app too, without query string.

Hmm — in app.handle, req.originalUrl is set by router at the top-level handle... Actually router sets req.originalUrl = req.originalUrl || req.url in its handle. For a mounted app, app.handle is called with req.originalUrl already set by the parent router. So in app.handle, req.originalUrl is available (top-level router sets it before calling layers; but app.handle is called from the router's layer, so originalUrl is set). Wait, for the top-level app, app.handle is invoked by http server directly (app as callback) — originalUrl is set inside this.router.handle. So at app.handle time before router.handle, originalUrl may be undefined at top-level. So we should compute path inside the wrapper (at the time done is called), where originalUrl is set. Use parseUrl.original(req).pathname, or req.originalUrl.

